        "anchor": "study-1",
        "title": "Study 1 — Blood sugar dips make you hungry",
        "image": "shopify://shop_images/Chocolate.jpg",
        "show_image_mobile": true,
        "background_heading": "The Study",
        "background_text": "1,070 people wore blood sugar monitors while eating over 71,000 real meals. The finding: it's not the sugar spike after a meal that makes you hungry — it's the crash that follows 2–3 hours later. The bigger the crash, the hungrier people got, the sooner they ate again, and the more they ate over the whole next day (Wyatt et al., 2021, Nature Metabolism).¹",
        "attributes_heading": "Study Attributes",
        "card_bg": "#ffffff",
        "title_bg": "#e4e8f4",
        "border_color": "#3447af",
