        "background_text": "GLP-1 medications (like semaglutide) produce big weight loss — but studies report that in some trials, 40–60% of the weight lost is muscle, not fat.⁵ And within a year of stopping, people regained about two-thirds of what they lost.⁶ Inositol is not a GLP-1 and its effects are far smaller — but in the trial above, the fat loss came with muscle kept or gained. Different tools for different jobs; talk to your doctor about what's right for you.",
